# {{ component.name }}

A minimal Next.js App Router + React + TypeScript full-stack scaffold. `/` is a static starting screen;
`GET /api/health` returns `{ "status": "ok" }`, not external-dependency or business-readiness status.
Authentication, databases, Server Actions, deployment policies and business features are not implemented.
Choose React/Vite for a browser-only SPA. Next.js does not require a separate NestJS app.

## Code and responsibilities

- `src/app/layout.tsx`: root document and shared page composition.
- `src/app/page.tsx`: static Server Component; introduce Client Components only at interactive boundaries.
- `src/app/api/health/route.ts`: HTTP Route Handler; keep server authority separate from client display state.
- `tests/health.test.mjs`: Node checks for handler status, headers and JSON, without a browser or Next server.

Keep secrets and server-only code out of the client module graph. Specify and test input, authorization, error and cache
contracts as features are added. Introduce `src/features` or shared modules for real cohesion/reuse, not empty layers.
There are no remote fonts, external APIs, storage or client state in the current scaffold.

## Environment and checks

Use Node 22.22.3 or later and npm 11.11.0. Each component owns its manifest and lock.

```sh
npm install
npm run check
```

Keep the generated `package-lock.json` in Git and use `npm ci` afterward. `check` runs `next typegen`, strict typechecking,
handler tests and a Next production build. Test `.ts` imports use supported Node native type stripping; this does not
replace Nest decorator compilation. Next generates `next-env.d.ts` and `.next/`.
`npm run dev` and, after building, `npm start` are separate loopback-only server commands on `127.0.0.1:3000`.
These checks do not establish browser/accessibility, product E2E or deployment behavior.

Official metadata pins checked on 2026-10-26: Next 16.4.3, React/react-dom 19.3.1, React types 19.3.0,
TypeScript 7.0.2 and Node 22 types 22.20.5. Review peers, Node, rendering compatibility and the lock when upgrading.
See [Next installation/App Router](https://nextjs.org/docs/app/getting-started/installation) and
[Next typegen](https://nextjs.org/docs/app/api-reference/cli/next#next-typegen-options).
Installed-version documentation is also available in `node_modules/next/dist/docs`.

